@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# scripts/
+
+The vigolium-side tooling this workflow relies on. Two scripts, one settings
+file, no upstream changes: everything here lives on the `local/stable` branch.
+
+## apply-settings.sh — reproduce the scan configuration
+
+A fresh vigolium install has defaults that are wrong for deep agentic scans:
+32 turns per run, a 10-minute call timeout, a 25-worker pace, and a stall
+detector that reads bash-based verification as "no progress". Those tweaked
+values are what this repo's scans run on, so they are kept in a file instead of
+in someone's shell history.
+
+```bash
+cd scripts
+./apply-settings.sh --check     # paired diff: vanilla install -> this machine
+./apply-settings.sh --dry-run   # the exact commands, changing nothing
+./apply-settings.sh             # apply (~1 min: one `config set` per key)
+./apply-settings.sh --verify    # do the current settings match the file?
+```
+
+`--check` materialises a pristine config in a temporary `HOME` and prints a
+per-key diff, so it is safe to run against a live install. It exits `3` when the
+two differ (they always will — that is the point of the file), `0` when they do
+not. Apply takes a minute because each key is a separate `vigolium config set`;
+`--verify` then re-reads the effective config and reports any key that did not
+stick.
+
+Secrets are deliberately absent from the settings file — `config set` stores
+them in cleartext in `~/.vigolium/vigolium-configs.yaml`. Set them once per
+machine:
+
+```bash
+vigolium config set agent.olium.custom_provider.api_key '<key>'
+vigolium config set oast.token '<token>'
+```
+
+## vigolium-settings.env — the values, one per line
+
+`KEY="value"` per line, `#` for comments. Every entry carries its vanilla
+default and what the knob actually does, because vigolium's own docs mostly do
+not. Sections: agent loop budget, provider, agent context limits, discovery,
+spidering/pacing, scope and phases, and a "repair" block for keys an older
+`config set` round-trip left null.
+
+Things worth knowing before editing it:
+
+- Unknown keys fail loudly (`key "…" not found: unknown config key`), so a typo
+  in a key name cannot silently do nothing.
+- Values are **not** validated consistently. `scope.cli_origin_mode` rejects
+  values outside `all|relaxed|balanced|strict`, but `agent.olium.autopilot_mode`
+  and `discovery.wordlists.tier` accept garbage and fall back to a default
+  without complaint. Check those two by hand.
+- `agent.olium.max_tokens` is honored by the Anthropic transports only; an
+  OpenAI-compatible provider ignores it.
+
+## check-findings.fish — independent re-check of existing findings
+
+Re-judges findings that are already in the project with a *different* model,
+without re-running the scan. Each finding is triaged alone (`vigolium agent
+triage <id>`) from captured traffic, so a second opinion costs one agent run per
+finding instead of a full scan.
+
+```bash
+./check-findings.fish                       # dry-run: render one triage prompt
+./check-findings.fish --run --models accounts/fireworks/models/glm-5p3,accounts/fireworks/models/ember-1
+./check-findings.fish --run --ids 9904,9918 --min-severity medium --models <id>
+./check-findings.fish --apply-consensus     # apply what every model agreed on
+```
+
+It refuses to check findings with the model that wrote them, skips checks that
+already have a verdict (so re-runs are free), and ends with a verdict-per-model
+table. `--apply-consensus` then batches the agreements into `vigolium finding
+mark` calls: unanimous confirmations, unanimous false positives, and a list of
+disagreements for a human.
+
+Discipline it enforces by construction: judging happens from captured traffic
+(`--no-probe` default, `--no-write` default), so a check pass changes nothing
+unless you pass `--probe` / `--write` / `--apply-consensus`.
+
+Raw output lands in `finding-checks/<model>/<id>.json` (verdict + reasoning) and
+`finding-checks/candidates.tsv`. Cost: roughly \$0.40 per check with a
+cache-heavy model on a dense finding set; `--help` shows how to sum the real
+token usage out of a run's transcript.
+
+A note from practice: model agreement is not correctness. In one pass GLM called
+a finding a false positive on solid source evidence while Ember confirmed it
+(and vice versa on another finding), so the *disagreements* are the valuable
+output — read them before trusting a clean table.
diff --git a/scripts/apply-settings.sh b/scripts/apply-settings.sh
new file mode 100755
index 00000000..fccc4d07
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/apply-settings.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,160 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# apply-settings.sh — put this machine's vigolium config into the state
+# scripts/vigolium-settings.env describes, or show how it differs from vanilla.
+#
+#   ./apply-settings.sh              apply the settings file  (~1 min: one
+#                                    `vigolium config set` per key)
+#   ./apply-settings.sh --check      paired diff: vanilla -> current
+#   ./apply-settings.sh --verify     do the current settings match the file?
+#   ./apply-settings.sh --dry-run    print the commands, change nothing
+#   ./apply-settings.sh --file F     use another settings file
+#   ./apply-settings.sh --help
+#
+# Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 failure or drift, 3 = --check found differences.
+#
+# --check builds a throwaway config in a temporary HOME, so it never touches
+# your real config or database.
+#
+# Secrets are not in the settings file. Set them once per machine:
+#   vigolium config set agent.olium.custom_provider.api_key '<key>'
+set -uo pipefail
+
+here=$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)
+file="$here/vigolium-settings.env"
+mode=apply
+
+usage() {
+    sed -n '2,19p' "$0" | sed 's/^# \{0,1\}//'
+    echo
+    echo "settings file: $file  ($(pairs 2>/dev/null | wc -l) keys)"
+}
+
+# Settings file -> "key=value" lines: comments and blanks dropped, surrounding
+# whitespace trimmed, surrounding double quotes removed (the file quotes values
+# so that [lists] survive; `config set` must not receive the quotes).
+pairs() {
+    grep -E '^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*=' "$file" | awk -F= '{
+        v = substr($0, index($0, "=") + 1)
+        sub(/[[:space:]]+#.*$/, "", v)
+        gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/, "", v)
+        if (v ~ /^".*"$/) v = substr(v, 2, length(v) - 2)
+        print $1 "=" v
+    }'
+}
+
+# Effective settings of the config in $HOME, as "key=value" lines.
+effective() {
+    vigolium config ls -j 2>/dev/null |
+        jq -r '.. | objects | select(has("key") and has("value")) | "\(.key)=\(.value)"' | sort
+}
+
+# Same, for a fresh install in a temporary HOME (never touches the real one).
+vanilla() {
+    local tmp; tmp=$(mktemp -d)
+    mkdir -p "$tmp/.vigolium"
+    HOME="$tmp" vigolium config ls -j 2>/dev/null |
+        jq -r '.. | objects | select(has("key") and has("value")) | "\(.key)=\(.value)"' | sort
+    rm -rf "$tmp"
+}
+
+# paired_diff <vanilla-file> <current-file>  -> "key  vanilla -> current"
+paired_diff() {
+    awk -F= '
+        NR == FNR { van[$1] = substr($0, index($0, "=") + 1); next }
+        { cur[$1] = substr($0, index($0, "=") + 1) }
+        END {
+            for (k in van) if (!(k in cur)) printf "%-46s %-26s -> (missing)\n", k, van[k]
+            for (k in cur) {
+                c = (k in van) ? van[k] : "(unset)"
+                if (cur[k] != c) printf "%-46s %-26s -> %s\n", k, c, cur[k]
+            }
+        }' "$1" "$2" | sort
+}
+
+# verify: every key in the settings file must equal the effective value.
+verify() {
+    command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "verify needs jq" >&2; return 1; }
+    local want have drift=0 total=0
+    want=$(pairs); have=$(effective)
+    while IFS= read -r line; do
+        [ -n "$line" ] || continue
+        total=$((total + 1))
+        key=${line%%=*}; val=${line#*=}
+        got=$(printf '%s\n' "$have" | grep -F "$key=" | head -1 | cut -d= -f2-)
+        if [ "$got" != "$val" ]; then
+            printf '  drift %-46s wanted %-22s have %s\n' "$key" "$val" "${got:-(missing)}"
+            drift=$((drift + 1))
+        fi
+    done <<< "$want"
+    if [ "$drift" -eq 0 ]; then
+        echo "verified: all $total key(s) match the settings file"
+        return 0
+    fi
+    echo "WARNING: $drift of $total key(s) did not stick"
+    return 1
+}
+
+while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
+    case "$1" in
+        --check)      mode=check ;;
+        --verify)     mode=verify ;;
+        --dry-run)    mode=dry ;;
+        --file)       shift; file=${1:-} ;;
+        --file=*)     file=${1#--file=} ;;
+        -h|--help)    usage; exit 0 ;;
+        *)            echo "apply-settings: unknown argument '$1' (--help)" >&2; exit 1 ;;
+    esac
+    shift
+done
+
+command -v vigolium >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "apply-settings: vigolium not on PATH" >&2; exit 1; }
+[ -r "$file" ] || { echo "apply-settings: cannot read $file" >&2; exit 1; }
+
+case "$mode" in
+check)
+    command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "apply-settings: --check needs jq" >&2; exit 1; }
+    cur=$(mktemp); van=$(mktemp)
+    effective > "$cur"; vanilla > "$van"
+    echo "vanilla: $(wc -l < "$van") keys   current: $(wc -l < "$cur") keys"
+    out=$(paired_diff "$van" "$cur")
+    n=$(printf '%s\n' "$out" | grep -c . || true)
+    echo "differences: $n"
+    echo
+    printf '%s\n' "$out"
+    rm -f "$cur" "$van"
+    [ "$n" -eq 0 ] || exit 3
+    ;;
+
+verify)
+    verify || exit 1
+    ;;
+
+dry)
+    echo "# would apply $(pairs | wc -l) setting(s) to ${HOME}/.vigolium/vigolium-configs.yaml"
+    pairs | while IFS= read -r line; do
+        printf 'vigolium config set %s %s\n' "${line%%=*}" "${line#*=}"
+    done
+    ;;
+
+apply)
+    ok=0; bad=0
+    while IFS= read -r line; do
+        [ -n "$line" ] || continue
+        key=${line%%=*}; val=${line#*=}
+        if out=$(vigolium config set "$key" "$val" 2>&1); then
+            ok=$((ok + 1)); printf '  ok   %-46s %s\n' "$key" "$val"
+        else
+            bad=$((bad + 1)); printf '  FAIL %-46s %s\n' "$key" "$val"
+            printf '       %s\n' "$(printf '%s\n' "$out" | tail -1)"
+        fi
+    done < <(pairs)
+    echo
+    echo "applied $ok setting(s), $bad failed"
+    echo
+    verify || true
+    echo
+    echo "secrets are not in the settings file; set them once per machine:"
+    echo "  vigolium config set agent.olium.custom_provider.api_key '<key>'"
+    [ "$bad" -eq 0 ] || exit 1
+    ;;
+esac
diff --git a/scripts/check-findings.fish b/scripts/check-findings.fish
new file mode 100755
index 00000000..4ab456a2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/check-findings.fish
@@ -0,0 +1,261 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env fish
+# check-findings.fish — re-check existing findings with other models, one at a
+# time, without re-running the scan. Run with --help for the full flag list.
+
+function usage
+    set -l b (set_color blue); set -l d (set_color normal); set -l g (set_color brblack)
+    echo "$b check-findings.fish $d— independently re-check findings with other models"
+    echo
+    echo "$b MODES $d"
+    echo "   (no --run)              dry-run: render one triage prompt. No model call, no writes."
+    echo "   --run                   check for real. Requires --models."
+    echo
+    echo "$b WHAT IT DOES $d"
+    echo "   Lists the project's confirmed/triaged findings at or above --min-severity"
+    echo "   and asks a model to judge each alone (vigolium agent triage): confirmed,"
+    echo "   false_positive or inconclusive. Ends with a verdict-per-model table, and the"
+    echo "   'vigolium finding mark' command for findings every model agreed on."
+    echo
+    echo "$b OPTIONS $d"
+    echo "   --models A,B            model id(s), e.g. accounts/fireworks/models/glm-5p3"
+    echo "                           required with --run; refuses the model that wrote the"
+    echo "                           findings (deepseek-v4p1-flash)"
+    echo "   --ids 9904,9918         check only these finding ids (default: all candidates)"
+    echo "   --min-severity LEVEL    high (default) | critical | medium | low | info"
+    echo "   --project UUID          default: the active project (~/.vigolium/active-project)"
+    echo "   --duration D            10m (default). A bare number means minutes (20 = 20m);"
+    echo "                           0 = no wall-clock limit (turn cap still applies)"
+    echo "   --outdir DIR            finding-checks (default)"
+    echo "   --only-operator         only findings from the operator agent (module_type=ai-agent)"
+    echo "   --probe                 let the model re-probe the live target (may change demo"
+    echo "                           state). Default is --no-probe: judge from captured traffic"
+    echo "   --write                 let verdicts change the finding status. Default is"
+    echo "                           --no-write: compare models without any status churn"
+    echo "   --apply-consensus       after the table, apply the verdicts every model agreed on"
+    echo "                           with one batched 'vigolium finding mark' per verdict;"
+    echo "                           disagreements and inconclusives are listed for you"
+    echo "   --by NAME               attribution for --apply-consensus (default independent-check)"
+    echo "   -h, --help              this screen"
+    echo
+    echo "$b EXAMPLES $d"
+    echo "   ./check-findings.fish"
+    echo "   ./check-findings.fish --run --models accounts/fireworks/models/glm-5p3"
+    echo "   ./check-findings.fish --run --ids 9904,9918,9905 --duration 0 --models m1,m2"
+    echo "   ./check-findings.fish --run --only-operator --models m1 --probe --write"
+    echo
+    echo "$b OUTPUT $d"
+    echo "   <outdir>/<model>/<id>.json   raw verdict document per check (resumable)"
+    echo "   <outdir>/candidates.tsv      the list that was checked"
+    echo
+    echo "$b COST $d"
+    echo "   every check gets its own agentic_scans row (mode=triage), but 0.5.3"
+    echo "   leaves token_usage empty on those rows — read the run transcript:"
+    echo "$g   jq -r '.message.usage? | select(.!=null) | [.input//0,.cacheRead//0,.output//0] | @tsv' \\"
+    echo "$g     ~/.vigolium/agent-sessions/<run-uuid>/transcript-agent-triage-confirm.jsonl$d"
+    echo "   sum the three columns over all rows; that reconciled with the provider"
+    echo "   bill (GLM 5.3: ~\$0.40 per check, ~93% of the input cached)"
+end
+
+argparse -n check-findings 'h/help' 'run' 'write' 'probe' 'apply-consensus' \
+    'models=' 'ids=' 'min-severity=' 'project=' 'duration=' 'outdir=' 'only-operator' 'by=' \
+    -- $argv
+or begin
+    usage
+    exit 2
+end
+if set -q _flag_h; or set -q _flag_help
+    usage
+    exit 0
+end
+
+set -l outdir $_flag_outdir
+if test -z "$outdir"
+    set outdir finding-checks
+end
+
+# A bare number is minutes: `--duration 20` is what people type, and a Go
+# duration without a unit does not parse at all.
+set -l duration $_flag_duration
+if test -z "$duration"
+    set duration 10m
+else if string match -qr '^[0-9]+$' -- $duration
+    set duration {$duration}m
+end
+
+set -l minsev $_flag_min_severity
+test -z "$minsev"; and set minsev high
+
+set -l P $_flag_project
+if test -z "$P"
+    set P (string trim -- (cat ~/.vigolium/active-project 2>/dev/null))
+end
+if test -z "$P"
+    echo "check-findings: no --project given and no active project" >&2
+    exit 1
+end
+
+set -l probe --no-probe
+if set -q _flag_probe
+    set probe
+end
+set -l write --no-write
+if set -q _flag_write
+    set write
+end
+
+# Only a *non-empty* id list filters. An empty-but-set variable must not.
+set -l ids
+if set -q _flag_ids
+    set ids (string split , -- (string join , $_flag_ids))
+end
+
+mkdir -p $outdir
+set -l manifest $outdir/candidates.tsv
+set -l sel '.items[]'
+if set -q _flag_only_operator
+    set sel '.items[] | select(.module_type == "ai-agent")'
+end
+vigolium --project-uuid $P finding --min-severity $minsev --verdict confirmed,triaged -j \
+    | jq -r "$sel | [.id, .severity, (.short // .module_id), .finding_hash, (.module_type // \"-\")] | @tsv" \
+    > $manifest
+or begin
+    echo "check-findings: could not list findings for project $P" >&2
+    exit 1
+end
+
+set -l n (count (cat $manifest))
+echo "project $P · $n candidate(s) at severity >= $minsev · outdir $outdir"
+
+if not set -q _flag_run; and not set -q _flag_apply_consensus
+    set -l first (string split \t -- (head -n1 $manifest))
+    echo "dry-run: rendering the triage prompt for #$first[1] ($first[2] $first[3])"
+    vigolium --project-uuid $P agent triage $first[1] --dry-run
+    echo
+    echo "nothing was sent and nothing was written. --run --models <id,...> checks for real; --help lists the flags."
+    exit 0
+end
+
+if not set -q _flag_models
+    echo "check-findings: --run needs --models, e.g. --models accounts/fireworks/models/glm-5p3 (see --help)" >&2
+    exit 1
+end
+set -l models (string split , -- (string join , $_flag_models))
+for m in $models
+    if string match -q '*deepseek-v4p1-flash*' -- $m
+        echo "check-findings: refusing to check findings with the model that wrote them ($m)" >&2
+        exit 1
+    end
+end
+
+for m in $models
+    set -l mname (string split , -- (string replace -a '/' ',' -- $m))[-1]
+    set -l mdir $outdir/(string replace -a '/' '_' -- $m)
+    mkdir -p $mdir
+    echo "== $mname"
+    set -l tocheck 0
+    for line in (cat $manifest)
+        set -l f (string split \t -- $line)
+        set -l id $f[1]
+        if test (count $ids) -gt 0; and not contains -- $id $ids
+            continue
+        end
+        set -l out $mdir/$id.json
+        if test -f $out; and jq -e '.items[0].verdict' $out >/dev/null 2>&1
+            echo "   skip #$id (already checked)"
+            continue
+        end
+        set tocheck (math $tocheck + 1)
+        echo "   → #$id $f[2] $f[3]"
+        vigolium --project-uuid $P agent triage $id \
+            --provider openai-compatible --model $m \
+            --max-duration $duration $probe $write -j > $out
+        or echo "     ✖ check failed for #$id (see $out)"
+    end
+    if test $tocheck -eq 0
+        echo "   nothing to check (all cached, or no id matched)"
+    end
+end
+
+echo
+set -l confirmed_hashes
+set -l fp_hashes
+set -l open_items
+printf '%-7s %-9s %-34s' id severity claim
+for m in $models
+    printf ' %-18s' (string split , -- (string replace -a '/' ',' -- $m))[-1]
+end
+echo
+for line in (cat $manifest)
+    set -l f (string split \t -- $line)
+    if test (count $ids) -gt 0; and not contains -- $f[1] $ids
+        continue
+    end
+    set -l verdicts
+    for m in $models
+        set -l mdir $outdir/(string replace -a '/' '_' -- $m)
+        set -a verdicts (jq -r 'if .ok == false then "failed" else (.items[0].verdict // "no verdict") end' $mdir/$f[1].json 2>/dev/null; or echo not-run)
+    end
+    printf '%-7s %-9s %-34s' $f[1] $f[2] (string sub -l 32 -- $f[3])
+    for v in $verdicts
+        printf ' %-18s' $v
+    end
+    echo
+    set -l uniq (printf '%s\n' $verdicts | sort -u)
+    if test (count $uniq) -eq 1
+        switch $uniq[1]
+            case confirmed
+                set -a confirmed_hashes $f[4]
+            case false_positive
+                set -a fp_hashes $f[4]
+            case '*'
+                set -a open_items "#$f[1] $f[2] → $uniq[1]"
+        end
+    else
+        set -a open_items "#$f[1] $f[2] → "(string join / $verdicts)
+    end
+end
+
+set -l by independent-check
+if set -q _flag_by
+    set by (string join ' ' $_flag_by)
+end
+
+echo
+if test (count $confirmed_hashes) -eq 0; and test (count $fp_hashes) -eq 0; and test (count $open_items) -eq 0
+    echo "no verdicts recorded yet — nothing to apply"
+    exit 0
+end
+
+set -l applyit 0
+if set -q _flag_apply_consensus
+    set applyit 1
+end
+
+if test (count $confirmed_hashes) -gt 0
+    set -l cmd vigolium --project-uuid $P finding mark $confirmed_hashes --as confirmed --by $by --note "independent check: every model agreed on confirmed"
+    echo "unanimous confirmed — $(count $confirmed_hashes) finding(s):"
+    echo "  "(string join ' ' -- (string escape -- $cmd))
+    if test $applyit -eq 1
+        $cmd; or echo "  ✖ mark failed"
+    end
+end
+if test (count $fp_hashes) -gt 0
+    set -l cmd vigolium --project-uuid $P finding mark $fp_hashes --as false_positive --by $by --note "independent check: every model agreed on false positive"
+    echo "unanimous false positive — $(count $fp_hashes) finding(s):"
+    echo "  "(string join ' ' -- (string escape -- $cmd))
+    if test $applyit -eq 1
+        $cmd; or echo "  ✖ mark failed"
+    end
+end
+if test (count $open_items) -gt 0
+    echo
+    echo "needs a human look — $(count $open_items) finding(s) with no agreement"
+    echo "  (re-run those ids with --probe, or check them with a second model):"
+    for x in $open_items
+        echo "    $x"
+    end
+end
+if test "$apply_consensus" = no
+    echo
+    echo "add --apply-consensus to run the mark commands above"
+end
diff --git a/scripts/vigolium-settings.env b/scripts/vigolium-settings.env
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5ce7156a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/vigolium-settings.env
@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@
+# vigolium-settings.env — the settings this setup runs on.
+#
+# Read by scripts/apply-settings.sh, applied with `vigolium config set`.
+# Format: KEY="value"   (quotes keep [lists] and spaces intact)
+#
+# Every knob that differs from a vanilla install is here, with its vanilla
+# default and what it actually does. Anything not listed is left at default.
+#
+# Secrets are deliberately NOT here (agent.olium.custom_provider.api_key,
+# oast.token, …). `config set` writes them into
+# ~/.vigolium/vigolium-configs.yaml in cleartext; set them by hand, once per
+# machine — see README.md.
+
+# ─── agent loop budget ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# Vanilla 32. One turn = one model response plus its tool calls. This is the
+# per-run hard cap, and it is what the `olium: exceeded max turns (32)` abort
+# comes from — the triage and query paths inherit it too.
+agent.olium.max_turns="400"
+
+# Vanilla 0 (provider default). Per-response *output* cap, honored by the
+# Anthropic transports only: an OpenAI-compatible endpoint (fireworks, ollama)
+# ignores it, so with the provider below this is effectively inert.
+agent.olium.max_tokens="1000000"
+
+# Vanilla 600. Deadline for a single model call. Ten minutes is not enough for a
+# long turn with a large context, and a call that hits it dies mid-run.
+agent.olium.call_timeout_sec="3600"
+
+# Vanilla 3 / 12. The loop closes a section after N consecutive turns with no
+# *productive* tool call and stops the run after M stall rotations in a row.
+# The progress detector only counts target-touching tools (run_native_scan,
+# web_fetch, send_raw_http, browser_probe, report_finding) — verifying through
+# bash: reading source, querying the target's database, replaying a request by
+# hand, reads as a stall. Raised because that is exactly this workflow.
+agent.olium.stall_rotations="5"
+agent.olium.stall_turns="20"
+
+# Vanilla "" (= legacy: no section rotation, report_finding writes findings
+# directly). shadow = bounded operator sections with context rotation, and every
+# report_finding is *also* mirrored into agent_finding_candidates so a
+# fresh-context verifier can grade them — findings still land immediately, the
+# mirror is what the FP-rate comparison reads. enforced = findings only via
+# propose_candidate → verify → promote. Unrecognized values fall back to legacy.
+agent.olium.autopilot_mode="shadow"
+
+# ─── model provider ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint; the vanilla default is a local ollama
+# (http://localhost:11434/v1, gemma4:latest). api_key is NOT here — see header.
+agent.olium.custom_provider.base_url="https://api.fireworks.ai/inference/v1"
+agent.olium.custom_provider.model_id="accounts/fireworks/models/deepseek-v4p1-flash"
+
+# ─── what the agent keeps in context ────────────────────────────────────────
+# Vanilla defaults, straight from the code: 50 findings, 100 endpoints, 20
+# high-risk items, risk score >= 50. Raised (and the risk bar lowered) so a deep
+# audit keeps most of the scan in view instead of silently dropping medium-risk
+# items. These four keys are not emitted by the default config at all — they
+# only exist once something sets them.
+agent.context_limits.max_findings="200"
+agent.context_limits.max_endpoints="400"
+agent.context_limits.max_high_risk="60"
+agent.context_limits.min_risk_score="30"
+
+# ─── discovery (deparos) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# Vanilla "auto". Which built-in wordlist tier discovery uses; valid values are
+# auto | short | long | large (note: only scope.cli_origin_mode is validated on
+# write, so a typo here is accepted silently). "large" is the widest.
+discovery.wordlists.tier="large"
+
+# Vanilla [] (dedup per path). Responses with these statuses collapse to ONE
+# representative per host instead of one per path: 401/403 auth-wall noise,
+# 429 rate limiting, 405/415/422 method/format noise.
+discovery.deparos_dedup.keep_one_per_host="[401, 403, 429]"
+discovery.deparos_dedup.keep_per_path="[405, 415, 422]"
+
+# Vanilla 4000. Cap on observed items held per discovery run.
+discovery.engine.observed_max_items="20000"
+
+# Vanilla 0 (derived from CPUs and RAM). Pinned so the embedded JS engine
+# (jstangle) has a predictable budget on a box that is also doing the scanning.
+discovery.jstangle.memory_budget_mb="768"
+
+# ─── spidering (spitolas) and pacing ────────────────────────────────────────
+# Vanilla 1500. Distinct crawler states one run may keep.
+spidering.max_states="5000"
+# Vanilla 50. Cap on extra route seeds one target's crawl browses. The config
+# does not document what 0 means; this install pins 0.
+spidering.max_extra_seeds="0"
+# Vanilla 25. Parallel requests per host.
+scanning_pace.concurrency="40"
+# Vanilla empty (no wall-clock limit). Stops spidering after this long.
+scanning_pace.spidering.max_duration="30m"
+
+# ─── scope and phases ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# Vanilla "balanced"; validated on write, must be all | relaxed | balanced |
+# strict. How scope filtering treats targets that came from the CLI (-t):
+# relaxed keeps more of what those targets lead to.
+scope.cli_origin_mode="relaxed"
+
+# Vanilla false. Enrich known-issue (template) scan targets with paths found in
+# earlier phases: more coverage, slower scan.
+known_issue_scan.enrich_targets="true"
+# Vanilla false. Same enrichment for the "lite" scanning strategy.
+scanning_strategy.lite.known_issue_scan="true"
+
+# Vanilla 1. API version the REST server serves when a client does not pin one.
+server.api_version_default="0"
+
+# Vanilla 1. Feedback rounds in the dynamic assessment phase: URLs discovered in
+# a round are fed back and re-scanned, up to N rounds.
+dynamic-assessment.max_feedback_rounds="3"
+
+# ─── repair: keys this config carried as null/"" ────────────────────────────
+# An older `config set` round-trip left these null or empty in
+# ~/.vigolium/vigolium-configs.yaml, so their effective value quietly came from
+# the code defaults. Pinning them to those documented defaults makes the
+# configuration explicit. Safe to delete this block if you prefer them unset.
+discovery.flush_interval="15s"
+discovery.stream_fuzz="true"
+discovery.sitemap.enabled="true"
+discovery.sitemap.follow_index="true"
+discovery.jstangle.persist_unreplayed="true"
+spidering.route_seeds="true"
+scanning_strategy.scan_logs.status_retention_days="30"
